WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.375
So what does the code add?

2
00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:03.812
A single new module and one entry script,

3
00:00:03.812 --> 00:00:08.612
which builds a plan by default and only
writes when you hand it an approved plan.

4
00:00:08.612 --> 00:00:13.099
It reuses the shared cloud table and
hashing from the earlier chapters

5
00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:16.976
but keeps its own client and
fakes, so nothing earlier changes.

6
00:00:16.976 --> 00:00:18.237
Two files drive it.

7
00:00:18.237 --> 00:00:23.013
The conversion file, kept by identity
engineering and reviewed with the application

8
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:25.771
owners, says what each
legacy credential becomes

9
00:00:25.771 --> 00:00:28.125
and which workload will present the token.

10
00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:30.397
And the cutover log, kept by the owner,

11
00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:34.630
records when each workload switched
and who approved the disable.
